239. Accordingly, invoking the U.N. and the practically nonexistent GSF as a basis to
terminate Haiti’s TPS is yet more pretext by Secretary Noem and the Trump administration.
240. Since taking office in January 2025, the administration has terminated every TPS
designation that it has reviewed. Specifically, the administration has terminated  or vacated the
following TPS designations:
• Venezuela, 90 Fed. Reg.  8805 (Feb. 3, 2025) (vacatur  of 2025 extension of 2023
designation);
• Venezuela, 90 Fed. Reg. 9040 (Feb. 5, 2025) (termination of 2023 designation);
• Haiti, 90 Fed. Reg. 10511 (Feb. 24, 2025) (partial vacatur);
• Afghanistan, 90 Fed. Reg. 20309 (May 13, 2025) (termination);
• Cameroon, 90 Fed. Reg. 23697 (June 4, 2025) (termination);
• Nepal, 90 Fed. Reg. 24151 (June 6, 2025) (termination);
• Haiti, 90 Fed. Reg. 28760 (July 1, 2025) (termination, later supplanted by November
28, 2025 termination);
• Nicaragua, 90 Fed. Reg. 30086 (July 8, 2025) (termination);
• Honduras, 90 Fed. Reg. 30089 (July 8, 2025) (termination);
• Venezuela, 90 Fed. Reg. 43225 (Sept. 8, 2025) (termination of 2021 designation);
• Syria, 90 Fed. Reg. 45398 (Sept. 22, 2025) (termination);
